WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.083
By the way I just have

2
00:00:01.083 --> 00:00:02.290
to ask you really quickly.

3
00:00:02.290 --> 00:00:03.730
Did you love doing Friends?

4
00:00:03.730 --> 00:00:04.620
Was that so fun?

5
00:00:04.620 --> 00:00:05.560
Cause that was like,

6
00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:07.340
that was all so so fun.

7
00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:08.940
I absolutely loved it.

8
00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:10.670
I was originally supposed

9
00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:11.503
to do three of 'em

10
00:00:11.503 --> 00:00:13.693
and it turned into nine shows

11
00:00:13.693 --> 00:00:16.040
and it's just a nice, positive,

12
00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:18.000
happy place with great actors.

13
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:20.120
Well, I loved you in that

14
00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:21.560
as well as so many other roles.

15
00:00:21.560 --> 00:00:26.030
Okay now, tell me about this #2020 Tip Challenge,

16
00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:27.290
Mr. Selleck.

17
00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:28.980
I read an article in the paper

18
00:00:30.569 --> 00:00:31.450
about my dear friend, Donnie,

19
00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:36.317
and he left this $2,020 tip,

20
00:00:36.317 --> 00:00:38.420
hoping for in the spirit

21
00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:41.590
of hoping for a better 2020.

22
00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:42.580
And started thinking about it

23
00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:44.970
and I talked to Jillie.

24
00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:47.030
I said, I guess we can afford it.

25
00:00:47.030 --> 00:00:47.870
I'm going to do this

26
00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:48.703
and she said,

27
00:00:48.703 --> 00:00:49.660
I think you should do it.

28
00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:53.420
And I go to this same restaurant most of the time

29
00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:55.060
and they're like family

30
00:00:55.060 --> 00:00:57.180
and everybody's hurting in New York.

31
00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:58.290
It's bad.

32
00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:03.120
So I wrote a little note and gave him a $2,020 tip

33
00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.776
and knew it might get around,

34
00:01:05.776 --> 00:01:08.850
but I didn't mind it in this case,

35
00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:11.070
not to say I'm a magnificent human being

36
00:01:11.070 --> 00:01:14.070
but to say, restaurants need help.

37
00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:16.910
Even if it's $20 and 20 cents,

38
00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:19.640
maybe you can help 'em out

39
00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:22.470
because they're really struggling

40
00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:24.820
maybe as hard hit as anything

41
00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:25.653
in this city.

42
00:01:25.653 --> 00:01:26.640
So.

43
00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:29.420
I love everything you just said.

44
00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:32.770
And this #2020 Tip Challenge,

45
00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:34.820
and I love that you gave the denomination

46
00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:36.840
of options for people

47
00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:39.270
because everybody has something different they can give.

48
00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:40.643
That is so fantastic.

49
00:01:40.643 --> 00:01:41.476
Yeah.

50
00:01:41.476 --> 00:01:43.580
And it has inspired us here

51
00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:45.140
at the show to pay it forward

52
00:01:45.140 --> 00:01:46.500
in honor of you and Donnie.

53
00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:49.090
And I was wondering if you would mind joining me

54
00:01:49.090 --> 00:01:51.990
in a Surprise Father-Daughter Drew Gooder.

55
00:01:51.990 --> 00:01:53.850
That's what we call them around here.

56
00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:55.380
They're a duo making a difference

57
00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:56.280
in their community.

58
00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:58.050
Would you do that with us?

59
00:01:58.050 --> 00:01:59.116
I'm here, man.

60
00:01:59.116 --> 00:01:59.949
(crowd applauds)

61
00:01:59.949 --> 00:02:02.930
Okay, so we like surprises around here

62
00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:03.763
so if it's okay,

63
00:02:03.763 --> 00:02:04.960
I'm going to hide you on zoom

64
00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:05.827
and then bring you back in.

65
00:02:05.827 --> 00:02:06.660
Oh, there you go.

66
00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:07.630
Perfect. Okay.

67
00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:09.950
We'll see you in a minute, Tom Selleck.

68
00:02:09.950 --> 00:02:13.333
Okay. Hello, Isabella and Luca!

69
00:02:14.698 --> 00:02:15.531
Hi-

70
00:02:15.531 --> 00:02:16.456
Hi Drew, Hi.

71
00:02:16.456 --> 00:02:17.855
So great to meet you.

72
00:02:17.855 --> 00:02:18.730
Nice to meet you.

73
00:02:18.730 --> 00:02:19.563
Oh my goodness,

74
00:02:19.563 --> 00:02:20.980
you're both so lovely.

75
00:02:20.980 --> 00:02:23.610
You're father and daughter.

76
00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:25.490
I love that you're a duo

77
00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:27.950
and I see you standing inside your restaurant,

78
00:02:27.950 --> 00:02:29.020
Tarallucci e Vino.

79
00:02:31.808 --> 00:02:32.641
Perfect.

80
00:02:32.641 --> 00:02:33.474
Thank goodness;

81
00:02:33.474 --> 00:02:35.020
I really went for it.

82
00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:37.160
And you guys have been working tirelessly

83
00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:39.450
to support frontline workers

84
00:02:39.450 --> 00:02:41.670
and what inspired you to do that?

85
00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:43.590
So it was really all inspired

86
00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:45.780
by an act of generosity

87
00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:48.090
from a family friend of ours.

88
00:02:48.090 --> 00:02:49.010
You know, we're obviously

89
00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:50.200
in the restaurant business

90
00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:52.570
and when the pandemic shut everything down

91
00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:53.710
in New York City

92
00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:55.250 line:15%
and our healthcare workers, you know, were

93
00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:57.730 line:15%
on the front lines, battling the virus

94
00:02:57.730 --> 00:02:58.563 line:15%
in the hospitals,

95
00:02:58.563 --> 00:02:59.396 line:15%
she reached and said,

96
00:02:59.396 --> 00:03:00.260 line:15%
I've been reading

97
00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:02.280 line:15%
what's been going on in the city.

98
00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:04.240
I'd love to help your guys' restaurant,

99
00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:05.073
but I'd also love

100
00:03:05.073 --> 00:03:06.010
for you to deliver food

101
00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:07.502
to an emergency room

102
00:03:07.502 --> 00:03:09.880 line:15%
because she knew how hard people were working.

103
00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:12.880 line:15%
So on March 19th last year,

104
00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:16.010 line:15%
my parents actually both delivered 40 meals

105
00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:17.730 line:15%
to the ER doctors and nurses

106
00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.100 line:15%
at NYU Langone Hospital

107
00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:22.170
on First Avenue, which is pretty close by actually.

108
00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:25.630
And the reaction from the doctors

109
00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:27.780
and nurses, they were so grateful.

110
00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:30.460
That's what inspired us to start feed the front lines.

111
00:03:30.460 --> 00:03:32.460
And I had just left college.

112
00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:33.660
You know, I was kicked off campus.

113
00:03:33.660 --> 00:03:37.080
I was about to graduate, but I told my friend

114
00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:37.913
about the idea

115
00:03:37.913 --> 00:03:39.680
and we built a website in 18 hours

116
00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:41.520
and started collecting donations

117
00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:43.170
and people were incredibly generous.

118
00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:44.910
So that's, that's really what inspired it.

119
00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:47.360
I mean, Luca, you must be so proud

120
00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:48.606
of your daughter.

121
00:03:48.606 --> 00:03:49.506
I could not have asked

122
00:03:49.506 --> 00:03:51.267
for a better daughter.

123
00:03:51.267 --> 00:03:52.360
She's amazing.

124
00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:55.959
And we have delivered over 170,000 meals

125
00:03:55.959 --> 00:03:58.290
but we brought on other restaurants,

126
00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:00.416
restaurants from all over New York

127
00:04:00.416 --> 00:04:04.640
and we've had over 35 restaurant partners.

128
00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:06.590
So it was not about Tarallucci e Vino,

129
00:04:06.590 --> 00:04:10.247
but it was about sort of trying to keep, you know

130
00:04:10.247 --> 00:04:12.090
New York restaurants alive

131
00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:14.751
because as you know, it's, it's been tough.

132
00:04:14.751 --> 00:04:15.584
It is still very tough.

133
00:04:15.584 --> 00:04:17.420
Well you're trying to inspire people

134
00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:18.800
and clearly you have.

135
00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:19.910
Now, ironically

136
00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:21.900
I hear someone that inspires you.

137
00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:23.633
You're a Tom Selleck fan?

138
00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:26.070
Yes, I am.

139
00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:27.020
Great, say hello

140
00:04:27.020 --> 00:04:28.602
to Mr. Tom Selleck.

141
00:04:28.602 --> 00:04:29.435
(crowd applauds)

142
00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:30.918
Wow!

143
00:04:30.918 --> 00:04:32.843
Hi there!

144
00:04:32.843 --> 00:04:34.493
Thanks for the work you're doing.

145
00:04:35.743 --> 00:04:36.576
Hi.

146
00:04:38.180 --> 00:04:39.285
This is incredible.

147
00:04:39.285 --> 00:04:40.590
I just thought that I should introduce you.

148
00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:43.123
I was Just hanging out, wanting to say Hi.

149
00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:46.810
So I grew up in Italy

150
00:04:46.810 --> 00:04:50.743
and I remember watching Magnum PI.

151
00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:54.573
You know?

152
00:04:54.573 --> 00:04:55.580
And he was the coolest guy.

153
00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:58.030
Is, still is the coolest guy out there

154
00:04:59.217 --> 00:05:00.680
and I think my mother was in love with him,

155
00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:01.513
you know?

156
00:05:01.513 --> 00:05:03.607
Oh, yeah, we all, everybody was!

157
00:05:03.607 --> 00:05:06.513
And Tom Selleck, who is such an amazing human being

158
00:05:06.513 --> 00:05:09.980
which is what really makes us love him,

159
00:05:09.980 --> 00:05:13.680
he has this #2020 Tip Challenge.

160
00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:17.520
And so on behalf of all of us here at the show

161
00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:20.790
we wanted to give you

162
00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:24.522
the #$2,020 tip

163
00:05:24.522 --> 00:05:28.470
that Tom and Donnie Wahlberg have been initiating.

164
00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:30.110
And of course, we're going to double that

165
00:05:30.110 --> 00:05:31.370
because there's two of you

166
00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:32.580
and then I'm going to throw in.

167
00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:35.100
So we're definitely going 10,000 here

168
00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:38.404
to just say thank you for everything

169
00:05:38.404 --> 00:05:40.510
that you are doing.

170
00:05:40.510 --> 00:05:41.550
We all wanna help

171
00:05:41.550 --> 00:05:43.500
but sometimes we don't know where to go.

172
00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:47.138
So I applaud you for leading the charge on this.

173
00:05:47.138 --> 00:05:47.971
Thank you so much.

174
00:05:47.971 --> 00:05:49.538
Stay well and prosper.

175
00:05:49.538 --> 00:05:50.500
Thank you so much.

176
00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:51.460
Appreciate it.

177
00:05:51.460 --> 00:05:53.270 line:15%
Wow. This is so generous.

178
00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:55.010 line:15%
Thank you both so much.

179
00:05:55.010 --> 00:05:55.930 line:15%
I am in awe of you.

180
00:05:55.930 --> 00:05:58.834 line:15%
That's all Drew; I'm outta money.

181
00:05:58.834 --> 00:06:00.650 line:15%
(everyone laughs)

182
00:06:00.650 --> 00:06:03.330
And yet, Tom, this is inspired by you

183
00:06:03.330 --> 00:06:04.490
and Donnie Wahlberg.

184
00:06:04.490 --> 00:06:06.230
And Isabella and Luca,

185
00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:08.860
you really are doing something incredible.

186
00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:11.830 line:15%
So for more information about Feed the Frontlines,

187
00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:14.870 line:15%
head to our website thedrewbarrymoreshow.com

188
00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:17.210 line:15%
to learn more and get involved yourself.

189
00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:18.150
Go New York!

190
00:06:19.125 --> 00:06:20.790
(crowd applauds)

191
00:06:20.790 --> 00:06:22.283
Thank you.

192
00:06:22.283 --> 00:06:25.130
All right, thank you Luca and Isabella.

193
00:06:25.130 --> 00:06:27.420
And Tom, thank you so much

194
00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:28.710
for coming on the show today.

195
00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:29.760
I really appreciate it.

196
00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:30.890
Thank you Drew.

197
00:06:30.890 --> 00:06:34.980
Thank you so much for giving us a lifetime of such goodness

198
00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:39.980
and Blue Bloods airs on Fridays ten, nine central on CBS.

199
00:06:40.553 --> 00:06:43.136 line:15%
